# WHY: the kb/ files are byte-compared by the kb-build golden test and hashed
# into the prompt-cache version (kbVersion). Git's core.autocrlf=true on Windows
# would materialise them as CRLF on checkout while kb-build always emits LF —
# so a fresh clone would fail the golden test and print a different kbVersion
# than the one recorded in progress.md. Pin the text formats to LF so the bytes
# are the same on every platform. (Narrow on purpose: a repo-wide `* text=auto`
# renormalisation is a separate chore.)
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
